{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516129-the-\u201cmuscle\u201d-isn\u2019t-a-retainer","id":1516129,"title":"The \u201cmuscle\u201d isn\u2019t a retainer?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-25T14:34:42-07:00","id":1516129,"title":"The \u201cmuscle\u201d isn\u2019t a retainer?","content":"So retainers are your daily living servants, but if you want someone with combat abilities, then you need an ally. But where does the guy who is the loyal muscle for your Mage fit in? He is under your chain of command, unlike an ally who is a peer, so why wouldn\u2019t he be a retainer do some sort?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T14:56:10-07:00","id":1516130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516129-the-\u201cmuscle\u201d-isn\u2019t-a-retainer#post1516129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So retainers are your daily living servants, but if you want someone with combat abilities, then you need an ally. But where does the guy who is the loyal muscle for your Mage fit in? He is under your chain of command, unlike an ally who is a peer, so why wouldn\u2019t he be a retainer do some sort?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say the muscle is a Retainer, but they\u2019re not nearly as useful or versatile as an Ally. If you interpret literally the rule that Retainers can\u2019t have any combat abilities at all, then they\u2019re not much good for anything except flavor text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T15:13:57-07:00","id":1516131,"title":"","content":"What do you think of the rule that (I think) came from V:tR saying that every dot you put into a retainer gives them a 10xp boost?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T15:14:21-07:00","id":1516132,"title":"","content":"Isn't it a matter of the quality of the muscle? A few mooks that a Heremetic found in poverty, because they had aged out of being mooks and lacked other job skills, and then he used Life Magic to heal their injuries and get them into fighting trim, they are still mooks/ retainers. High competence mooks with restored physical capabilities, but mooks.<br /> <br /> Now, the retired Mercenary that runs a gym and teaches boxing and other forms of fighting, she's an ally to the Heremetic. She's a much more widely competent person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T16:01:41-07:00","id":1516141,"title":"","content":"And what of an ex marine that a Hermetic with Life 3 and Mind 4 found living penniless on the streets with pieces of his body and mind missing which he put back together with his magic? The marine is a faithful retainer, but perhaps he requires 5 dots in Retainer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T16:06:15-07:00","id":1516143,"title":"","content":"It's a possibility. Remember, if you want to make the person you healed either a retainer or an ally, respect and compassion always.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T08:15:37-07:00","id":1516458,"title":"","content":"This is why I like the retainer background from Vampire as it states the retainer could be highly capable and skilled in many things. In M20, your retainer literally cannot do anything combat related if taken literally and seems to be useful only for social or mental rolls and being a glorified man/woman servant, butler, or maid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","user":"Starcomet","date":". 07-03-2023, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T08:30:25-07:00","id":1516460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516129-the-\u201cmuscle\u201d-isn\u2019t-a-retainer?p=1516143#post1516143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a possibility. Remember, if you want to make the person you healed either a retainer or an ally, respect and compassion always.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who needs respect and compassion when you can just brainwash them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T10:21:26-07:00","id":1516478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516129-the-\u201cmuscle\u201d-isn\u2019t-a-retainer?p=1516460#post1516460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who needs respect and compassion when you can just brainwash them</div> </div> </div> </div>Brainwashing always backfires. Respect and compassion are by far the surer bet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T10:46:03-07:00","id":1516484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1516129-the-\u201cmuscle\u201d-isn\u2019t-a-retainer?p=1516478#post1516478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Brainwashing always backfires. Respect and compassion are by far the surer bet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say &quot;always&quot;. Sometimes, yes.<br /> <br /> But by &quot;brainwashing&quot;, I dont mean just the extremely invasive act of actively shaping the memories and thoughts of the poor guy to your like. A &quot;simple&quot; emotional manipulation may be enough. Many people dont truly understand how powerful a &quot;simple&quot; Mind 2 effect can be. Make the target become obsessive in love with you, or develop a fanatic devotion towards &quot;the cause&quot;. You can implant all those feelings in the target with a simple Mind 2 effect that dont involve straping the person in a chair on room 101 and leaving him with strange nightmares for the rest of his life, or some massive plethora of other strange and inconvenient mental quirks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}